{# The person card under the tabs, the same on every page: portrait, name,
   job title and claim, so a visitor knows whose site this is before reading
   anything else.

   Embed it, and fill `more` for an introduction that runs on the name's
   column; the card then carries no right column. Without `more` the card
   closes on the right with “Nachricht schreiben”, unless `reach` is false.

   The portrait is shown in black and white by the stylesheet, never by
   editing the photograph, and is never mirrored. The soft hyphen lets
   “Softwareentwickler” break on a phone; “Senior” has none and stays whole.
   The claim breaks after its first sentence at every width, so the punch
   line stands on its own. Where even the first sentence is too wide—beside
   the phone portrait below 360 pixels—“mit Hut.” moves down together rather
   than leaving “Hut.” alone.

   Params: reach (default true). Block: more. #}
{%- set reach = reach ?? true -%}
{%- set more -%}{% block more %}{% endblock %}{%- endset -%}
<section class="card cover{% if more|trim is not empty %} cover-has-more{% endif %}" aria-label="Marcel Kraus">
    <span class="cover-face"><img src="{{ asset('images/portrait.jpg') }}" alt="Porträt von Marcel Kraus" width="576" height="720"></span>
    <div class="cover-who">
        <h1 class="text-t2 font-bold">Marcel Kraus</h1>
        <p class="text-t3">Senior Software&shy;entwickler iOS/Web</p>
    </div>
    <p class="cover-claim text-t3 text-muted">Nicht nur mit&nbsp;Hut.<br>Mit Köpfchen.</p>
    {% if more|trim is not empty %}
        <div class="cover-more">{{ more }}</div>
    {% elseif reach %}
        <div class="cover-reach">
            {{ include('partials/_link.html.twig', { href: path('app_contact_page'), label: 'Nachricht schreiben', to: 'page', class: 'button' }, with_context = false) }}
        </div>
    {% endif %}
</section>
